 #:seon.task{:name "declared-metadata-selects-a-value-that-no-longer-fits"
            :plan "(select-keys (`seon.db/pull` db '[*] [:seon.fn/name 'x/y]) [:q]) is {} but prints as \"Error evidence is unavailable.\": select-keys keeps the refusal's metadata {`:seon.error/declared-schema` `:seon.db/invalid-read-error`}, and render selection (`seon.render/declared-producers`) takes that declaration's pair without asking whether the value still satisfies it (the validator answers false). Law tension (root 2026-09-28): AGENTS says the producer declares identity and nothing downstream guesses, and entity_pairs_test asserts a declaration selects even when the value does not fit, so validating at selection was not landed. Fix at the derivation instead (a derived value must not carry its source error declaration), or bring the rule to the owner. Read `seon.render/request-projection` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/mcp-dogfood--patches--render--01-declared-schema-must-fit.patch`."}
