 #:seon.task{:name "a-timeout-or-load-dependent-render-outcome-is-never-reused-by-read-evidence"
             :plan "Commit 35cafc1dc made `seon.render/render-call` keep every invocation in the `:seon.render/invocation` `seon.cache` kind, refusals and timeouts included, valid while its read evidence is current. A timeout, or any outcome that depends on load or time rather than on what the render read, is not a value of what was read: it must stay a typed unknown (never a cached result) until unrelated reads change, so a render that timed out under load is evaluated again on the next call. Deterministic refusals (a contract refusal, a thrown map) may stay cached. Change the owner, `seon.render/render-call`: decide at the point where the invocation outcome is produced whether it is cacheable, from its error type, not by a filter beside the cache. Proof: to write before assignment, a deftest naming this task whose first `seon.render/render-call` times out (a renderer exceeding its bound) and whose second call with the same read evidence runs the renderer again, plus one case showing a deterministic refusal is reused. Read `seon.render/render-call` and `seon.cache`."}
